The idea: strip the page down to one calm accent and generous empty space, then let the small info cards sit like stones on still water — muted until you touch them. I kept your grid and widgets untouched; the weather, todo, notes, countdown and greeting need to be added as widgets in the editor (the pack validates and previews the look, and the layout stays as you have it).

A calm deep-sea dusk: I've kept your teal palette but cooled the background toward a darker navy-teal, gave the clock a serif voice so it reads as the focal point, and let the search bar and icon tiles echo the accent only faintly so nothing competes with the time. No layout changes — your clock, date, search and websites stay exactly where they are.

