A calm off-white light theme: serif clock, roomy spacing, and a muted teal accent carried only by the search focus ring and the icon hover.

I left out the tracking pixel on purpose — the pack rules forbid external `url()` references, so a remote image can't be loaded from the theme CSS. If you want tab-open counts, a local counter in the extension (or a service that works with a data: approach) would be the way to go.

I can't load the remote font or wallpaper: external `url()` calls (and `@font-face` pointing at a remote file) are rejected by the validator, and image links aren't allowed in a pack. Instead, this uses the closest built-in display face (`cormorant`, an editorial serif) and a deep ink gradient; upload your own mountain photo as wallpaper and set `background.dim` to taste.

